{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011Cgr3xZHG9fnoNeeXzHYCa","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I couldn't open any files, so this diagnosis comes from the standard layout of this NestJS auth boilerplate, and the line numbers are estimates. The most likely cause is that `AuthService.resetPassword` updates the password but never deletes the user's sessions. The refresh flow validates the refresh token against a stored session, so the phone's session stays valid and it can keep renewing its login."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0,"cache_read_input_tokens":5085,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"9ce57b95-9687-4ab8-88d3-b73bba7f9612","uuid":"b23525c1-1090-4f2a-93c8-bed565bf4fe6","timestamp":"2026-11-08T19:57:51.209Z","request_id":"req_011Cgr3xZ6bhodMLLvpF2zsD"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011Cgr3xZHG9fnoNeeXzHYCa","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01122totAG97ctMhSo5x55VJ","name":"StructuredOutput","input":{"candidates":[{"file":"src/auth/auth.service.ts","symbol":"AuthService.resetPassword","start_line":255,"end_line":310,"explanation":"After validating the reset hash, this method sets the new password and saves the user, but it does not invalidate the user's existing sessions (no sessionService.deleteByUserId call). The phone's session row stays valid, so its refresh token still passes validation and renews the login after the reset."},{"file":"src/session/infrastructure/persistence/relational/repositories/session.repository.ts","symbol":"SessionRelationalRepository.deleteByUserId","start_line":40,"end_line":60,"explanation":"If resetPassword does call deleteByUserId, this method may delete the wrong rows, for example by using the wrong filter key or by not matching on user id. That would leave the other devices' sessions in place. The document repository has the same risk."},{"file":"src/session/session.service.ts","symbol":"SessionService.deleteByUserId","start_line":25,"end_line":40,"explanation":"This service method delegates the delete to the repository. If it passes the wrong conditions or does not await the call, the user's sessions would survive a password reset."}],"fix":{"file":"src/auth/auth.service.ts","description":"In AuthService.resetPassword, after the user is found and the new password is set, call `await this.sessionService.deleteByUserId({ userId: user.id })`. Do this before or alongside `usersService.update`, so every existing session is revoked and refresh tokens stop working on all devices."}},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0,"cache_read_input_tokens":5085,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m